prompt:
Design the complete file structure and implementation order.

Plugin name: {{plugin_name}}
Target directory: {{target_dir}}
Architecture modules: {{spec-reader.architecture_modules}}
Schemas: {{spec-reader.schemas}}
Hooks: {{spec-reader.hooks}}
Risk matrix: {{risk-assessor.risk_matrix}}
Phases: {{risk-assessor.phases}}
Node min version: {{node_min_version}}

Your task:
1. Design a production-ready file structure (tree format)
2. Identify 4-8 core files/modules (config, entry point, schema definitions, hook handlers, etc.)
3. For each core file, list its purpose and dependencies (which files must exist first)
4. Order files by dependency (topological sort): foundational first, dependent files last
5. Suggest a README outline (what sections are needed)
6. Identify test structure (unit, integration, e2e)
7. Create a package.json template snippet (if Node.js)

Return JSON:
{
  "directory_tree": "",
  "core_files": [
    {"path": "src/index.ts", "purpose": "", "dependencies": [], "phase": 1}
  ],
  "file_order": [],
  "readme_sections": [],
  "test_structure": {"unit_dir": "", "integration_dir": "", "test_files": []},
  "package_json_template": {},
  "config_files": []
}
